course: dictionary
lesson: 4618
title: Higher: comparing two things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Higher is the comparison form of high. You use it when you put two things side by side and one is further up than the other. «A ship sits a little higher in the sea than in a river.» Higher here means the ship sits up a little more out of the water.
explain: Higher can mean further up from the ground, bigger in number, or more advanced. Ask yourself: higher than what? Look for the word than, or for the second thing being compared. «Move up to higher floors» compares floors with the ground floor, and «a higher score» compares one score with another.
explain: Try the word in the sentence. Swap in a word like more or further up, and see if the sentence still makes sense. «Rivers always flow from higher land to lower land» still works with more up, so higher is the right word.
fact: Higher is the comparative of high: high, higher, highest.
fact: Higher means more high, further up from the ground than something else.
fact: Higher can mean bigger in number or amount, as in «a higher score» or a higher price.
fact: A higher sound is sharper and thinner, like a whistle.
fact: «Rivers always flow from higher land to lower land», so a river flows away from the mountains. Higher land is usually colder.
exercise: «Rivers always flow from higher land to lower land.» Where does a river start its flow? | From the bottom of the sea | *From the higher land | From the lower land | From the middle of the sea
exercise: «In a flood, move up to higher floors and never walk in floodwater.» What should you do in a flood? | Stay on the ground floor by the window | *Go up to a higher floor, away from the water | Walk through the floodwater to find help | Swim in the fast water
exercise: «Sam's score is higher than Mia's score.» What does higher mean here? | *More in number | Further from the ground | Lower and sadder | Thinner, like a whistle
test:
«A whistle makes a higher sound than a drum.» What does higher mean for a sound? | *Sharper and thinner | Louder and deeper | Shorter in time | Quieter
Coach says, «Aim higher next time.» What does aim higher mean? | *Try for something better and more advanced | Aim your ball at the ground | Look up at the sky | Stop trying
exam:
In «higher maths», what does higher mean? | Lower and easier | *More advanced | Further up the hill | Louder
